⚡ Vite Configuration
vite.config.js needs CORS proxy for local development:

export default {
  server: {
    port: 5173,
    proxy: {
      '/api': {
        target: 'http://localhost:8080',
        changeOrigin: true,
      }
    }
  }
}

This lets you call /api/auth/login from frontend and Vite proxies it to the API Gateway.
🔐 Auth Flow
1. Login
User submits form → POST /api/auth/login → Backend returns {token, role, userId, name}
2. Store
AuthContext stores token in localStorage + React state. Sidebar re-renders with role-based links.
3. Request
Every API call: axios interceptor reads token from localStorage → adds Authorization: Bearer header.
4. Logout
Click logout → clear localStorage → reset AuthContext → navigate to /login.
